ChromiumPortable — third-party components, trademarks, and redistribution
=======================================================================

This repository (MIT) contains a portable-build toolchain that patches
Chromium-family browsers with Chrome++ (version.dll injection). The toolchain
source is MIT-licensed. Browser binaries, Chrome++, and brand names are not.

1. Productized distribution (Chrome / Edge / Helium)
---------------------------------------------------
Release practice and public product pages are limited to these three channels
and their dedicated child repositories. That status is a project policy choice,
not a claim that upstream licenses permit redistribution.

2. Other Chromium-family browsers (capability only)
---------------------------------------------------
Opera, Vivaldi, Brave, Thorium, 360 极速浏览器 X, and similar browsers
may be built by this toolchain (auto layout + optional GitHub Actions). Builds
of those browsers, when published as GitHub Release assets from this core, are:

  - UNOFFICIAL and not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the
    corresponding browser vendors;
  - not presented as products of ChromiumPortable (no download-site product
    cards, no brand logos in the product gallery);
  - subject to each upstream's license / EULA, which may forbid or restrict
    redistribution of installers or modified binaries.

If you publish such builds, YOU are the redistributor. Evaluate the upstream
terms first. Prefer local/personal builds (`scripts/build_all_packages.py`,
`build-packages`) and avoid implying official status.

